cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying manuscript, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Diatom-TDI: deep learning estimation of the Trophic Diatom Index from light microscopy images"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end, offline pipeline that estimates the Kelly & Whitton Trophic
  Diatom Index from light microscopy images. A fine-tuned EfficientNet-B3
  classifies 101 benthic diatom taxa, a budget-aware sliding-window detector
  converts whole micrographs into cell counts, and the published
  abundance-weighted index is computed with planktonic taxa excluded. The
  repository also quantifies how single-cell classification error propagates
  into the assemblage-level index and releases a slide-grouped split for
  leakage-free retraining.
